% M8-bits-encoding (D-0153): PB conflict analysis over rows whose every term is on the bits
% encoding at --bits-above 0, with a BITS pivot. Satisfiable (x = y = 4, w = 7, z = 3), so
% every atom's `red` pair is checked over a database that does not prove everything.
%
% Nothing is decided at the root: x + y + w >= 15 leaves each of x, y, w at least 1, and
% the two rows through z leave z <= 6. The search takes z first, at its maximum. z = 6
% pushes x <= 1 and y <= 1 (each through a row with a bits term on both sides), and the
% third row then needs w >= 13: a conflict two propagations deep. PB analysis instantiates
% the conflict row at x <= 1, y <= 1 (the atoms x_ge_2, y_ge_2) and w at its declared high,
% resolves on each atom against its reason instantiated at that atom, and learns a row
% over z's atom (z <= 5). The same happens at z = 5 and z = 4; z = 3 lands.
var 0..7: x :: output_var;
var 0..7: y :: output_var;
var 0..7: w :: output_var;
var 0..7: z :: output_var;
constraint int_lin_le([1, 1], [x, z], 7);
constraint int_lin_le([1, 1], [y, z], 7);
constraint int_lin_le([-1, -1, -1], [x, y, w], -15);
solve :: int_search([z, x, y, w], input_order, indomain_max, complete) satisfy;
